From 0c6970b3bbf60865c0061114184072a53c0ab609 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 06:30:07 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(js): checkVisibility counts an inline svg's drawn content
 as having boxes

checkVisibility() treated an element without a layout rect as having no box.
The shapes, groups, text and nested svgs inside an inline <svg> are drawn by
the SVG renderer within the root's box and get no rect of their own, so all
of them read invisible where Chrome reports them visible (a click target
like <svg><a>...</a></svg> was skipped). An SVG element under a root that
has a box now generates one unless it or an SVG ancestor computes
display:none. Compared with Chrome on 40 elements: inline svg content now
matches; still differing are content-visibility:hidden (not implemented),
empty inline elements on an empty line (no rect yet), <stop>, and
foreignObject content (not rendered).

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
